Operator: 'crack tn36 L3's path mechanic and solve it.' DONE.

THE PATH MECHANIC: L3 has two WALL obstacles (bizgpiltwm) at x~45-48 covering
y[20,32) and y[4,16), leaving a GAP at y[16,20). cwtesiybfx (tn36.py:2269) reverts
any move that collides with a wall, so a straight 'all-ups-then-rights' fails (it
ends up inside an obstacle). The object must route THROUGH the gap: up into y=16,
cross x=45 at y=16, then to the target. Winning order [33,2,2,2,33,2].

GENERAL SOLVER upgrade: compute the move MULTISET from deltas, then SEARCH orderings
(the game is the path oracle) until one wins -- two-pass (discover the winning order
per level, then clean minimal replay on a FRESH env, since env.reset() does NOT
rewind an advanced episode). Now reproduces L1-L3 (reproduced=True claimed_level=3,
25 clicks). Registry: tn36 levels_reproduced 2->3, reproducible_total 17->18.

L4 frontier: computes [3,3,3,3,1,9] (downs+left+SCALE-down) but no ordering wins ->
L4 adds scale<->collision interaction (object box changes size mid-path). Logged.
